      <activity id="1c2c19fa-d34c-5fb7-ab7c-91f52b3b6b97" activityNameId="6c50f693-e41d-5791-948a-dd0858434d7e" activityNameContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83" type="1" specialActivityType="0" energyValues="0">
        <activityName xml:lang="en">Heat, residential, by combustion of hydrogen using CHP, allocated by exergy, distributed by pipeline, produ [e1a5250786]</activityName>
        <generalComment>
          <text xml:lang="en" index="1">Full activity name: Heat, residential, by combustion of hydrogen using CHP, allocated by exergy, distributed by pipeline, produced by Electrolysis, AEC using electricity from grid
This dataset represents the supply of 1 megajoule of heat in a residence, by hydrogen combustion in a CHP. The hydrogen is produced by  Electrolysis, AEC, with electricity from grid as feedstock. Heat conversion efficiency [% LHV input]: 41.7%. LHV [MJ/kg]: 120. Market price [Euro/MJ]: 0.03. Synthesis efficiency [% LHV input]: 0%. Total cap. Input-related [kW]: 443.9. CO2 biogenic share [%]: 0%. Power [kW]: 200. Lifetime [years]: 19.51. Annual operation [hours]: 4100. Allocation factor: 0.08. On-site storage loss [%]: 0. Use loss [%]: 0.5. For more information, refer to: Sacchi, R. and Bauer, C. LCA of Power-to-X processes and applications in the residential sector. Paul Scherrer Institut, 2023. Source: Sacchi, R. and Bauer, C. LCA of Power-to-X processes and applications in the residential sector. Paul Scherrer Institut, 2023.

 UUID: dfda9de4-acb0-390e-bd0c-bb0654b6ffb5
Location: 
Technology: 
Time period: 
Production volume: 
Sampling: Sampling procedure: Literature data
Extrapolations: 
Uncertainty adjustments: 
BAFU mapped export: unsupported biosphere exchanges excluded; see audit/. Local UUIDs and generic activity classification are export conventions. Source: process_dfda9de4-acb0-390e-bd0c-bb0654b6ffb5.xml</text>
        </generalComment>
      </activity>
